-- title:
--   Trichotomy for points of the base-changed Deligne–Rapoport model
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0$ be a nonzero natural number and $q$ a prime with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a package of type `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN` for the curve `DRLevel.X N₀ q` over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring `DRLevel.R q`, the structure morphism being `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q`; among the data recorded by such a package are an open subset `𝔛.smoothLocus` of `DRLevel.X N₀ q` and, for an algebraically closed residue field, two morphisms `𝔛.comp κ _ 0` and `𝔛.comp κ _ 1` into the corresponding fibre. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, $\rho_O \colon \mathrm{R}\,q \to O$ a ring homomorphism, and assume the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by the image of $q$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Write $X_O :=$ `DRLevel.XO ρO` for the fibre product of `DRLevel.toBase N₀ q` with $\operatorname{Spec}(\rho_O)$, with projections `DRLevel.XO.toBase ρO` $=$ `pullback.snd` to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ and `pullback.fst` to `DRLevel.X N₀ q`. Then every point $x$ of $X_O$ satisfies at least one of: $x$ lies in the preimage under `DRLevel.XO.toBase ρO` of the basic open set $D(q) \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} O$; $x$ lies in the preimage under `pullback.fst` of `𝔛.smoothLocus`; or $x =$ `𝔛.crossingPt ρO toκ n` for some point $n$ of the fibre product of `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` and `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 1`, that is, $x$ is the image of $n$ under `pullback.fst` followed by `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` followed by `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`.
--
--   This is the point-set form of the Deligne–Rapoport description of the reduction at $q$ of the modular curve of level $N_0q$ after base change to a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $q$: outside the generic fibre, a point either lies in the smooth locus or is one of the finitely many crossing points of the two components of the geometric fibre. It is used in the verification that the local rings of the base-changed model at points other than the crossing points are regular ([`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_forall_ne_crossingPt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_forall_ne_crossingPt)).
